    {
     "type": "codeBlock",
     "attrs": {
      "language": "typescript",
      "localId": "96ff12b5ac6a"
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "const { data, isLoading, isValidating, setSize, error, size } = useSWRInfinite(\n  shouldFetch ? getUrl : null,\n  openmrsFetch,\n  { keepPreviousData: true },\n);"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "This keeps the banner list mounted across query changes. With stable "
      },
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "key={patient.uuid}",
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "code"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": ", React reuses banners for patients still in the new results, so no remount → no fan-out → no main-thread stall. "
      },
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "isLoading",
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "code"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": " then stays false on subsequent searches (only true on the very first load), and the loader gates in the view components don't tear down the subtree. "
      },
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "isValidating",
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "code"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": " can drive a non-disruptive loading hint if one is desired."
      }
     ],
     "attrs": {
      "localId": "d21864d2406e"
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "heading",
